        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0815" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg753"/>

                <head>No. 435.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boker to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 20, 1877</date>.
                        (Received Jan. 10, 1878.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I nave the honor to forward to yon herewith
                    a short article from the Journal de St. Petersburg, of this date, upon the
                    Russian budget of 1876, with a translation of the same. There were no doubt very
                    considerable expenditures made in that year in anticipation of the war which
                    broke out in the spring of 1877, and Russia has therefore reason to congratulate
                    herself that the expenditures exceeded the receipts by so small an amount. As
                    soon as I receive in an official form the compte rendu for 1876, I shall have
                    the honor to forward it to you.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. H. BOKER.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d440-a1.xml" xpointer="d440-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
